speciationNote  "phenylurea: no ionizable group in the ambient pH window, so rejection is steric plus strongly polar (the carbonyl gives a high dipole moment) rather than Donnan.";
applicationNote "the least-retained member of the atrazine / simazine / diuron NF benchmark set despite a comparable molar mass -- a near-linear shape and a high dipole moment lower its effective steric rejection.  The comparison is qualitative here; no rejection number is stored on a component.";
